sxml-qt4 list - List test cases with their environments and applicability

Usage: sxml-qt4 list [--catalog=FILE] [--spec=SPEC] [--test-set=NAME] [TEST-LIST]

Reads the QT4 catalog with sxml's XML parser and writes each selected
test case: its query file, its environment (sources, parameters,
namespaces, static base URI, resources, collections) with file paths
relative to the catalog's directory, its dependencies, and, when it
cannot run for SPEC, "skip:" and the reason. The selection is the
test cases of TEST-LIST, those of the test set --test-set names, or
with neither every test case of the catalog. Exits 1 when a test set,
test case or environment does not exist, 3 when a file cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --catalog=FILE   The catalog.xml of the suite (default: third_party/qt4tests/catalog.xml)
      --spec=SPEC      The language and version the run targets (one of: XP40, XQ40; default: XP40)
      --test-set=NAME  Select every test case of one test set

Arguments:
  TEST-LIST  File naming test cases, one '<test-set> <test-case>' per line

Examples:
  sxml-qt4 list tests/qt4/torture-slice.txt
  sxml-qt4 list --test-set=fn-abs
  sxml-qt4 list --catalog=suite/catalog.xml --spec=XQ40
